# Keeps the build context small and secrets out of the image.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .` in its builder stage, so anything not listed
# here is sent to the daemon and can land in a layer. What must NOT be added:
# prisma/ (the schema and the migrations the entrypoint replays),
# docker-entrypoint.sh, prisma7.config.ts, and the app's config files - the
# build fails without them.

# dependencies and build output: reinstalled and rebuilt inside the image
node_modules
.next
out
build
coverage

# secrets - every .env form, including .env.local and any .env.backup-*.
# Credentials reach the container through compose at run time, never a layer.
.env
.env.*

# version control and CI
.git
.gitignore
.github

# local tooling and editors
.claude
.vscode
.idea
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# caches and logs
.turbo
.swc
*.tsbuildinfo
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# docs and compose files: read on the host, never needed in the image
*.md
docker-compose*.yml
.dockerignore

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
